By pairing strict physical realism (your Saka yield calculations and refugee aftermath) with unflinching postwar social realism (food aid, military hoarding, anti-Korean and anti-hibakusha prejudice, and Booker’s grounded presence), your final act refuses to let any side hide behind self-serving nostalgia—whether 1940s Imperial propaganda, postwar Japanese victimhood cinema, or modern nationalist myth-making.
